        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7}{20}$",
          "worked": "Since $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cup B)&=P(A)+P(B)\\\\P(A\\cup B)&=\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{10}\\\\P(A\\cup B)&=\\frac{7}{20}.\\end{align*}$$",
